<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Commands on kevin</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/</link><description>Recent content in Commands on kevin</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>run</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/run/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/run/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-run"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-run"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Starts the &lt;code&gt;env&lt;/code&gt; steps in dependency order and waits. On Ctrl-C, it removes the steps in reverse order. A second Ctrl-C quits at once and leaves the rest for the next run to clean up. Removal stops after 5 minutes.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;With &lt;code&gt;--detach&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;-d&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;run&lt;/code&gt; starts in the background, prints the console and proxy addresses, and returns. Stop it with &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/stop/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin stop&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>setup</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/setup/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/setup/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-setup"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin setup&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-setup"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Starts the &lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt; steps in dependency order, and leaves them running after it exits. Use &lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt; for something that many &lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt;s share, such as a kind cluster. Remove the steps with &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/teardown/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin teardown&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin setup&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin setup --open&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Flag&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: center"&gt;Type&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: center"&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--open&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;bool&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;open the console in the default browser once it&amp;rsquo;s listening&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/environment-file/"&gt;Environment file&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>teardown</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/teardown/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/teardown/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-teardown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin teardown&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-teardown"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Removes the &lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt; steps, in reverse dependency order.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin teardown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>init</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/init/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/init/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-init"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin init&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-init"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Downloads and extracts each plugin package that a step uses, and verifies its signature if the entry sets &lt;code&gt;signing&lt;/code&gt;. It does not start plugins or check the environment file against their schemas. Use &lt;code&gt;kevin validate&lt;/code&gt; for that.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin init&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prints the qualified name of every plugin it fetched, one per line.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>validate</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/validate/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/validate/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-validate"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin validate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-validate"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Checks the environment file: its fields, each step&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;with&lt;/code&gt; block against the schema of its step type, &lt;code&gt;needs&lt;/code&gt; references, and &lt;code&gt;${...}&lt;/code&gt; expressions. It starts the plugins to read their schemas, but creates nothing and does not need a container engine.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin validate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prints the project name and the setup/env step counts on success.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>plugin</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/plugin/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/plugin/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-plugin"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin plugin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-plugin"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Packages, publishes, finds, and trusts plugins. See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/third-party-plugins/"&gt;Third-party plugins&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/extending/publishing-a-plugin/"&gt;Publishing a plugin&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="kevin-plugin-pack-dir"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin plugin pack &amp;lt;dir&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-plugin-pack-dir"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Creates a plugin package (&lt;code&gt;.tar.gz&lt;/code&gt;) from the files in &lt;code&gt;dir&lt;/code&gt;, and writes its &lt;code&gt;manifest.json&lt;/code&gt;. If &lt;code&gt;dir&lt;/code&gt; has a &lt;code&gt;manifest.json&lt;/code&gt;, the flags replace its fields. If it has none, the flags must supply every field.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin plugin pack ./my-plugin -o my-plugin.tar.gz&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;table&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Flag&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: center"&gt;Type&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: center"&gt;Default&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;th style="text-align: left"&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/thead&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;tbody&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--args&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;stringSlice&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;default arguments for the entrypoint (overrides manifest.json)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--author&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;plugin author (overrides manifest.json)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--description&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;plugin description (overrides manifest.json)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--entrypoint&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;entrypoint path, relative to dir (overrides manifest.json)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--name&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;plugin name (overrides manifest.json)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--output&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;-o&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required.&lt;/strong&gt; output tar.gz path&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;&lt;code&gt;--version&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;&lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: center"&gt;-&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;td style="text-align: left"&gt;plugin version (overrides manifest.json)&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;/tr&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/tbody&gt;&#10;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="kevin-plugin-push-targz-oci-ref"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin plugin push &amp;lt;tar.gz&amp;gt; &amp;lt;oci-ref&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-plugin-push-targz-oci-ref"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Uploads a plugin package to an OCI registry, with the credentials from &lt;code&gt;docker login&lt;/code&gt;. If &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;tar.gz&amp;gt;.minisig&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;tar.gz&amp;gt;.sigstore.json&lt;/code&gt; exists, &lt;code&gt;push&lt;/code&gt; uploads it too. The registry keeps one signature for each package, so push only one of them.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ca</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/ca/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/ca/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-ca"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin ca&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-ca"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Manages the kevin root CA in the trust stores of this machine. It does not need a project: every project on the machine uses the same root CA. See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/guides/ca-and-trust/"&gt;Trust the kevin CA&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="kevin-ca-install"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin ca install&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-ca-install"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Creates the kevin root CA if it does not exist, then adds it to the trust stores of this machine: the macOS keychain or the Linux CA directory, and the certificate database of each Firefox profile. A trust store that is not on the machine is skipped. Running it again is safe.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>do</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/do/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/do/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-do-name----extra-args"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin do &amp;lt;name&amp;gt; [-- extra args...]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-do-name----extra-args"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Runs a command from the &lt;code&gt;commands&lt;/code&gt; block of the environment file. kevin reads the outputs of the steps in the command&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;needs&lt;/code&gt;, fills in the &lt;code&gt;${...}&lt;/code&gt; expressions in &lt;code&gt;run&lt;/code&gt;, and replaces itself with the command. Arguments after &lt;code&gt;--&lt;/code&gt; are appended to &lt;code&gt;run&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin &lt;span class="k"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt; shell&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin &lt;span class="k"&gt;do&lt;/span&gt; migrate -- --dry-run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The steps in &lt;code&gt;needs&lt;/code&gt; must be up, and their step types must support export. See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/environment-file/#commands"&gt;Environment file: commands&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>doctor</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/doctor/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/doctor/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-doctor"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin doctor&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-doctor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Checks that the container engine is reachable, that the kevin root CA is trusted, and, if the project directory has an environment file, that its proxy and console ports are free. It changes nothing.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin doctor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prints one line per check: &lt;code&gt;ok&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;fail (reason)&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;skip (reason)&lt;/code&gt;. Exits&#10;non-zero if any check reports &lt;code&gt;fail&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>stop</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/stop/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/stop/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-stop"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin stop&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-stop"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Stops a running &lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt; for this project and environment, as Ctrl-C would, and waits for it to exit. Does nothing if kevin is not running.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin stop&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/run/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s&#10;&lt;code&gt;--detach&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;-d&lt;/code&gt; flag.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>status</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/status/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/status/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-status"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin status&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-status"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Prints the state of each step of a running &lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt;, as the console shows it. Prints &lt;code&gt;not running&lt;/code&gt; if kevin is not running for this project and environment.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;kevin status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/logs/"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin logs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for the output of a step.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>logs</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/logs/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/logs/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-logs"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin logs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-logs"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Prints the output of a step. With no step name, it prints the output of every step, in order. It works while &lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt; is running and after it exits, including after a crash.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;kevin also writes every log line as JSON, including debug lines, to &lt;code&gt;kevin.log&lt;/code&gt; in the project state directory (&lt;code&gt;.kevin/&lt;/code&gt; by default).&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>rerun</title><link>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/rerun/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://justenwalker.github.io/kevin/docs/reference/commands/rerun/</guid><description>&lt;!-- Code generated by cmd/gen-docs commands from kevin's cobra command tree and reference.md.tmpl. DO NOT EDIT. --&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="kevin-rerun"&gt;&lt;code&gt;kevin rerun&lt;/code&gt;&lt;a class="anchor" href="#kevin-rerun"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Reruns one step of a running &lt;code&gt;kevin run&lt;/code&gt;, the same as the console&amp;rsquo;s rerun button. It returns once the rerun finishes, prints the state of the step and of any other step that changed, and exits nonzero if the step failed. It fails if the step does not exist or is already running, and if kevin is not running for this project and environment. Interrupting the command cancels the rerun.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>